<title>USA: Pa. defeats plan to charge towns for police costs.</title>
<headline>Pa. defeats plan to charge towns for police costs.</headline>
<dateline>HARRISBURG, Pa. 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Legislature defeated a proposal to charge 22 communities in western Pennsylvania for state police protection.</p>
<p>The proposal, by Gov. Tom Ridge, would have affected communities with populations in excess of 9,000 to reimburse the state for police services.</p>
<p>The townships argued that they need the protection but could not afford the cost.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
